{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>This heap.</b> They drove a sword into the heap also as testimony. Therefore Balaam was punished by both, as we say: 'He is Laban, he is Beor, he is Cushan-Rish'ataim' — for such is the way of liars and falsifiers to be stricken by means of the witnesses. And Balaam was stricken by the heap, as it is written: ״ותלחץ רגל בלעם אל הקיר״, and that wall was the heap; and by the sword, as it is written: ״ואת בלעם בן בעור הרגו בחרב״. And likewise we find in the case of a young man who betrothed a young woman and swore to her that he would not marry another upon her, and he gave her as testimony a weasel and a pit. After some days he married another, and she bore him two sons — one the weasel dragged away, and one fell into the pit. It turns out he was punished by his witnesses. And there is support for this from what is written: ״יד העדים תהיה בו בראשונה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:24.195668604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}